{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>בדד</b> – a noun that falls upon both masculine and feminine, with a lamed and in its absence, and likewise the word בטח:" "<b>רבתי, שרתי</b> – milra, to distinguish between the added yod and the yod of the speaker-sign, like: אויבתי לי (Micah 7:8), אהבתי לדוש (Hosea 10:11). And the word גנובתי יום stands milra, because of the change of the bet:" "<b>רבתי בגוים</b> – it is not like the first, but in the language of greatness, like: ורבי המלך (Jeremiah 41:1), על כל רב ביתו (Esther 1:8). And it is punctuated with a lamed in למס to indicate the demonstrative heh that is missing. And the mem was not given a dagesh to lighten the burden on the tongue:"], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:27.526406044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}